CORE
array_of_structs_loop2.sv
--bound 1
^\[main\.p0\] .*: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p1\] .*: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p2\] .*: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p3\] .*: PROVED up to bound 1$
^\[main\.p4\] .*: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
As array_of_structs_loop1, with 64 elements, and with a member read of
an element written by the previous iteration. Reads of members and
elements of an aggregate value select the parts that hold the bits,
rather than extracting the bits from the flattening of the entire value;
otherwise, the expressions grow with the cube of the number of elements,
and this test runs out of memory.
